WEBVTT

00:00:02.450 --> 00:00:05.450
Most games of Catan are
decided before the first roll,

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:08.160
by where you place your
first two settlements.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:11.240
Catan Lens helps you get
that decision right.

00:00:11.929 --> 00:00:14.119
Every board follows the official setup.

00:00:14.469 --> 00:00:18.789
Catan Lens scores every legal corner, and
the gold ring marks the strongest one

00:00:18.809 --> 00:00:19.639
still open.

00:00:20.446 --> 00:00:23.416
The card beside the board says
what that corner produces.

00:00:23.866 --> 00:00:25.006
Open "Why this corner?"

00:00:25.026 --> 00:00:28.536
for the reasoning in plain
English: how much it yields,

00:00:28.586 --> 00:00:32.136
which resources, and whether
they are rare on this board.

00:00:32.894 --> 00:00:34.384
Curious about another spot?

00:00:34.914 --> 00:00:38.604
Click any corner for a grade,
its share of the best score,

00:00:38.674 --> 00:00:40.524
and exactly what it is missing.

00:00:41.342 --> 00:00:45.962
Keep the best corner instead, and the ring
moves to the second settlement that best

00:00:45.982 --> 00:00:47.252
completes your first.

00:00:48.109 --> 00:00:52.379
Practise with sixteen drill levels, or
copy the real board from your table.

00:00:52.569 --> 00:00:56.319
It all runs in your browser,
with no account and no tracking.

00:00:57.445 --> 00:00:58.535
Catan Lens.

00:00:58.825 --> 00:01:02.175
Free, open source, and
ready for your next game.
